---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import "../../styles/docs.css";

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
const image = (name: string) => `${base}images/guides/${name}.png`;
---

<Base
	title="Transaction Inspector | Actual Budget Tweaks"
	description="See a transaction's payee history, rules and schedule in a side panel."
>
	<main class="docs center">
		<header class="docs__header stack stack--sm">
			<a href="/guides" class="docs__back">Back to guides</a>
			<h1>Transaction Inspector</h1>
			<p class="docs__lead">
				Transaction Inspector shows a transaction's payee history, the rules for that payee and its
				schedule in a side panel. Use it to check whether a charge looks right or to find out why a
				transaction got its category.
			</p>
		</header>

		<section class="docs__section">
			<h2>Inspecting a transaction</h2>
			<p>Turn on Transaction Inspector in the Accounts &amp; Transactions section of Tweaks, then:</p>
			<ol>
				<li>Open an account and click <strong>Inspect</strong> in its toolbar.</li>
				<li>
					Tick a transaction's checkbox. The panel follows your selection, and if you tick several it
					shows the newest one you ticked.
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p>
				The sidebar collapses while the panel is open. Click <strong>Inspect</strong> again or close
				the panel to bring it back.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="docs__section">
			<h2>Reading the panel</h2>
			<div class="docs__stage docs__stage--card">
				<img
					src={image("inspector")}
					width="340"
					height="711"
					alt="The Inspector panel for a City Power bill marked 28% above usual, with its payee history, the Power bill schedule and two rules"
				/>
			</div>
			<p>
				The top of the panel shows the transaction's details. A badge such as
				<strong>+28% vs usual</strong> appears when the amount is at least 25% away from the payee's
				average, once the payee has three or more transactions. Badges also mark splits and transfers.
			</p>
			<p>
				<strong>Payee history</strong> shows the average amount, how often the payee usually charges
				you and the six most recent transactions across all accounts.
			</p>
			<p>
				<strong>Schedule</strong> appears if the transaction is linked to one, with its next date.
			</p>
			<p>
				<strong>Rules for this payee</strong> lists each rule in plain words, with rules created by
				schedules listed separately. The pencil opens the rule or schedule in Actual's editor.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="docs__section">
			<h2>Finding a transaction that doesn't match your rules</h2>
			<div class="docs__stage docs__stage--card">
				<img
					src={image("inspector-rules")}
					width="340"
					height="420"
					alt="The Inspector panel for a Fuel Stop charge, warning that rules would change its category from Fun to Transport"
				/>
			</div>
			<p>
				<strong>Your rules would change</strong> appears when running your rules now would give the
				transaction a different result. Rules run when a transaction is added, so this usually means
				someone edited it by hand or it was added before the rule existed. The panel only reports the
				difference and doesn't change the transaction.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="docs__section">
			<h2>Creating a rule</h2>
			<p>
				<strong>Create rule from this</strong> opens Actual's rule editor with the payee and category
				filled in. Nothing is saved until you save the rule there.
			</p>
		</section>
	</main>
</Base>
